A||N||4||bHooper||brake problem?||||5||
Z||000000||bHooper||03-07-2000||08:56 AM||||hey guys, i have a question about brakes.  this guy, that i work with, has a 84 SE.  when you work the brakes, there is an <B>extreme amount of stiffness in the pedal</B>... i also noticed, when you press the brake pedal, the voltage drops slightly????  i do not understand this at all.<P>does anyone have any thoughts on these problems?<P>thanks,<BR>brian  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||03-07-2000||09:29 AM|||| Make sure that all the calipers slide freely. As for the voltage drop- just a guess - batt. could be getting weak and if the engine is not running you will see a drop because of the brake lights.<p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 03-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||03-07-2000||09:49 AM||||if the brake booster has a problem, like a plug/crushed vac line or even a bad booster, the pedal will be really hard.<P>The brake master cyl also need checking... If there's allot of metal flake in the fluid there is some kind of problem. likely one or more cylinders binding.<P>As for the lights. check all the ground ties and battery cables. The voltage is droping because you just switched on 4 rather hot lamps. Usually you don't see the drop verry visibly. If the needle is moving more than a fraction then you have loose wire someplace.||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||03-07-2000||10:03 AM||||thanks, i will have him check out your suggestions.<P>i know for a fact that there is a fair amount of grinding on the left front rotor, also the battery has been replaced in the past couple of months.<P>brian||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dan||03-07-2000||07:44 PM|||| For sure check all 4 corners. If you try to make 3 wheels do the work of 4, the pedal pressure is extremely. I also highly recommend the 91 Baretta brake upgrade. ||||reg||1
